<title>GREECE: CITIBANK CUTS BASE LENDING RATE BY 75 BASIS POINTS.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK CUTS BASE LENDING RATE BY 75 BASIS POINTS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will cut its base rates</p>
<p>for working capital loans and freely investible funds by 75</p>
<p>basis points. Its business and professional base lending rate</p>
<p>will also come down 50 basis points, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 17.50 from 18.25</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 18.50 from 19</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 17.75 from 18.50</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 16.75 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans at 24 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 23 percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Rates on working capital loans in foreign currency for the</p>
<p>coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  8.04 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.65 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  3.06 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.57 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.60 percent</p>
<p>    Pounds Sterling:  9.18 percent</p>
<p>    French francs  :  5.87 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss francs   :  4.40 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
